                <pb facs="0709" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115/14287: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at London</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-21T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                                1918—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Consult Embassy regarding its No. 1418, August 27, 5 p.m. Take matter up with
                    Procurator General at once, and ascertain what proofs he required in addition to
                    those already presented to establish American ownership of goods not sold and
                    whether speedy determination of questions of title may be expected, with a view
                    to effecting delivery of goods to American owners at earliest possible
                    moment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
